  "cut_point": "We are given a **pocket calculator** that can display **up to eight significant digits**, and we are to find the **largest integer** $ n $ such that the **sum of the first $ n $ positive integers** (i.e., $ 1 + 2 + 3 + \\ldots + n $) **does not exceed 8 digits** (i.e., is less than or equal to $ 10^7 $)",
  "reflection": {
    "verified_state": [
      "The task is to find the largest integer n such that the cumulative sum 1+2+...+n can be displayed on an eight-digit calculator without scientific notation."
    ],
    "error_step": "(i.e., is less than or equal to $ 10^7 $)",
    "error_reason": "This incorrectly equates an eight-digit display limit with 10^7. An eight-digit display can show integers up to 99,999,999, so the correct bound is < 10^8 (or ≤ 99,999,999), not ≤ 10^7.",
    "new_direction": "Set up the inequality n(n+1)/2 < 10^8 (or ≤ 99,999,999) and solve for the largest integer n."
  }
